  "body": "## Summary\n- keep normal bot sessions fail-closed when a stored `bot-X.json` cannot be restored\n- prevent the legacy `BotContext` recovery path from silently switching to `createContext(null)` after a storage-state restore failure\n- leave the saved session file untouched so a transient Playwright restore problem cannot turn a logged-in bot into a fresh browser session\n- preserve the original Playwright error as suppressed diagnostic information\n\n## Scope\nOnly `BrowserManager` changes. Market observer, login logic, CAPTCHA handling, workers, negotiations, and session file format are untouched.\n\n## Expected behavior\n- normal bot with valid stored session: unchanged\n- bot without any stored session: clean first-login context still works\n- anonymous market observer: clean anonymous context still works\n- existing stored session that fails to restore: the job fails instead of silently opening a clean context",
